-- title:
--   Toric m-torsion subgroup as closure of toric points
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, that is, the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over `base p` carrying a relative group law, together with identifications of `JZero N₀` with the sections of $X$ over the generic point and of `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` with the sections over the residue point. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, and let $m$ be a natural number with $0 < m$. The assertion is that the subgroup $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ of `JZero (N₀ * p)` equals the additive subgroup generated by the image of the map $\chi \mapsto O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m\,hm\,\chi$, where $\chi$ runs over the $A$-algebra homomorphisms from `muCoord A O.toricRank m` to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, each such $\chi$ giving the point of `JZero (N₀ * p)` obtained, through the identification `O.pts`, from the composite of the character point `muPt A O.toricRank m χ` with the toric lift `O.toricLift m hm`, transported to the generic fibre along $\Lambda.h\sigma_A$.
--
--   This is the definitional interface for the toric part of the $m$-torsion of the Néron object of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$: since `toricPts` is defined by a case split on whether $m$ is positive, the lemma records the value on the positive branch. It is used by the results on the Hecke eigenplane in the Tate module of $J_0$ at $p$ and on membership in the toric subgroup under reduction conditions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_toricPts_of_pos.lean

